lass assignment</h4><p>Complete Applied case 6 and defend which resources are actually available to the estate.</p><p><a href=\"#case-6\">Open the applied case</a></p><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/estate-and-gift-taxes\">IRS estate and gift tax resources</a></p>"},{"id":"cfp-class-7-1","title":"Course 7 · Class 1 · Open the Rivera capstone","html":"<h3>Course 7 · Class 1 · Open the Rivera capstone</h3><p><a href=\"#capstone\">Course syllabus</a> · <a href=\"#cfp-class-7-2\">Next class</a></p><h4>Two-hour class</h4><ol><li>10 minutes · Recall what you learned in the previous class or identify what you already know.</li><li>35 minutes · Learn the concepts using the linked topic lessons. Answer each knowledge check before revealing the answer.</li><li>25 minutes · Work through the linked topic questions. Write down the rule, inputs and interpretation.</li><li>10 minutes · Break.</li><li>30 minutes · Complete the class assignment. Explain what changes if an assumption is wrong.</li><li>10 minutes · Explain your conclusion aloud, log anything you missed and mark the class complete.</li></ol><h4>Teaching and worked practice</h4><ul><li><a href=\"#topic-7\">Open Topic 7</a></li><li><a href=\"#topic-69\">Open Topic 69</a></li></ul><h4>Class assignment</h4><p>Write engagement scope, questions for the first meeting and an assumptions log.</p><p><a href=\"#capstone\">Open the Rivera capstone and rubric</a> · <a href=\"#workbook\">Open the advisor worksheets</a></p><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.cfp.net/certification-process/education-requirement/certification-coursework-requirement/the-capstone-course\">CFP Board capstone guidance</a></p>"},{"id":"cfp-class-7-2","title":"Course 7 · Class 2 · Verify the case facts","html":"<h3>Course 7 · Class 2 · Verify the case facts</h3><p><a href=\"#cfp-class-7-1\">Previous class</a> · <a href=\"#capstone\">Course syllabus</a> · <a href=\"#cfp-class-7-3\">Next class</a></p><h4>Two-hour class</h4><ol><li>10 minutes · Recall what you learned in the previous class or identify what you already know.</li><li>35 minutes · Learn the concepts using the linked topic lessons. Answer each knowledge check before revealing the answer.</li><li>25 minutes · Work through the linked topic questions. Write down the rule, inputs and interpretation.</li><li>10 minutes · Break.</li><li>30 minutes · Complete the class assignment. Explain what changes if an assumption is wrong.</li><li>10 minutes · Explain your conclusion aloud, log anything you missed and mark the class complete.</li></ol><h4>Teaching and worked practice</h4><ul><li><a href=\"#topic-8\">Open Topic 8</a></li><li><a href=\"#topic-9\">Open Topic 9</a></li></ul><h4>Class assignment</h4><p>Create the balance sheet and cash-flow statement. Reconcile every amount to the case.</p><p><a href=\"#capstone\">Open the Rivera capstone and rubric</a> · <a href=\"#workbook\">Open the advisor worksheets</a></p><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.cfp.net/certification-process/education-requirement/certification-coursework-requirement/the-capstone-course\">CFP Board capstone guidance</a></p>"},{"id":"cfp-class-7-3","title":"Course 7 · Class 3 · Rank the goals and test alternatives","html":"<h3>Course 7 · Class 3 · Rank the goals and test alternatives</h3><p><a href=\"#cfp-class-7-2\">Previous class</a> · <a href=\"#capstone\">Course syllabus</a> · <a href=\"#cfp-class-7-4\">Next class</a></p><h4>Two-hour class</h4><ol><li>10 minutes · Recall what you learned in the previous class or identify what you already know.</li><li>35 minutes · Learn the concepts using the linked topic lessons. Answer each knowledge check before revealing the answer.</li><li>25 minutes · Work through the linked topic questions. Write down the rule, inputs and interpretation.</li><li>10 minutes · Break.</li><li>30 minutes · Complete the class assignment. Explain what changes if an assumption is wrong.</li><li>10 minutes · Explain your conclusion aloud, log anything you missed and mark the class complete.</li></ol><h4>Teaching and worked practice</h4><ul><li><a href=\"#topic-10\">Open Topic 10</a></li><li><a href=\"#topic-12\">Open Topic 12</a></li><li><a href=\"#topic-65\">Open Topic 65</a></li></ul><h4>Class assignment</h4><p>Compare a reserve-first plan with a split reserve and debt plan.</p><p><a href=\"#capstone\">Open the Rivera capstone and rubric</a> · <a href=\"#workbook\">Open the advisor worksheets</a></p><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.cfp.net/certification-process/education-requirement/certification-coursework-requirement/the-capstone-course\">CFP Board capstone guidance</a></p>"},{"id":"cfp-class-7-4","title":"Course 7 · Class 4 · Prepare the risk recommendation","html":"<h3>Course 7 · Class 4 · Prepare the risk recommendation</h3><p><a href=\"#cfp-class-7-3\">Previous class</a> · <a href=\"#capstone\">Course syllabus</a> · <a href=\"#cfp-class-7-5\">Next class</a></p><h4>Two-hour class</h4><ol><li>10 minutes · Recall what you learned in the previous class or identify what you already know.</li><li>35 minutes · Learn the concepts using the linked topic lessons. Answer each knowledge check before revealing the answer.</li><li>25 minutes · Work through the linked topic questions. Write down the rule, inputs and interpretation.</li><li>10 minutes · Break.</li><li>30 minutes · Complete the class assignment. Explain what changes if an assumption is wrong.</li><li>10 minutes · Explain your conclusion aloud, log anything you missed and mark the class complete.</li></ol><h4>Teaching and worked practice</h4><ul><li><a href=\"#topic-18\">Open Topic 18</a></li><li><a href=\"#topic-20\">Open Topic 20</a></li><li><a href=\"#topic-25\">Open Topic 25</a></li></ul><h4>Class assignment</h4><p>Produce a coverage inventory and estimate the family’s protection gap.</p>