impact</h3><p><a href=\"#cfp-class-7-5\">Previous class</a> · <a href=\"#capstone\">Course syllabus</a> · <a href=\"#cfp-class-7-7\">Next class</a></p><h4>Two-hour class</h4><ol><li>10 minutes · Recall what you learned in the previous class or identify what you already know.</li><li>35 minutes · Learn the concepts using the linked topic lessons. Answer each knowledge check before revealing the answer.</li><li>25 minutes · Work through the linked topic questions. Write down the rule, inputs and interpretation.</li><li>10 minutes · Break.</li><li>30 minutes · Complete the class assignment. Explain what changes if an assumption is wrong.</li><li>10 minutes · Explain your conclusion aloud, log anything you missed and mark the class complete.</li></ol><h4>Teaching and worked practice</h4><ul><li><a href=\"#topic-37\">Open Topic 37</a></li><li><a href=\"#topic-40\">Open Topic 40</a></li><li><a href=\"#topic-41\">Open Topic 41</a></li></ul><h4>Class assignment</h4><p>Compare incremental tax and cash availability for two funding options.</p><p><a href=\"#capstone\">Open the Rivera capstone and rubric</a> · <a href=\"#workbook\">Open the advisor worksheets</a></p><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.cfp.net/certification-process/education-requirement/certification-coursework-requirement/the-capstone-course\">CFP Board capstone guidance</a></p>"},{"id":"cfp-class-7-7","title":"Course 7 · Class 7 · Model retirement outcomes","html":"<h3>Course 7 · Class 7 · Model retirement outcomes</h3><p><a href=\"#cfp-class-7-6\">Previous class</a> · <a href=\"#capstone\">Course syllabus</a> · <a href=\"#cfp-class-7-8\">Next class</a></p><h4>Two-hour class</h4><ol><li>10 minutes · Recall what you learned in the previous class or identify what you already know.</li><li>35 minutes · Learn the concepts using the linked topic lessons. Answer each knowledge check before revealing the answer.</li><li>25 minutes · Work through the linked topic questions. Write down the rule, inputs and interpretation.</li><li>10 minutes · Break.</li><li>30 minutes · Complete the class assignment. Explain what changes if an assumption is wrong.</li><li>10 minutes · Explain your conclusion aloud, log anything you missed and mark the class complete.</li></ol><h4>Teaching and worked practice</h4><ul><li><a href=\"#topic-44\">Open Topic 44</a></li><li><a href=\"#topic-45\">Open Topic 45</a></li><li><a href=\"#topic-52\">Open Topic 52</a></li></ul><h4>Class assignment</h4><p>Run a baseline and a stress case. Explain the trade-offs in client language.</p><p><a href=\"#capstone\">Open the Rivera capstone and rubric</a> · <a href=\"#workbook\">Open the advisor worksheets</a></p><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.cfp.net/certification-process/education-requirement/certification-coursework-requirement/the-capstone-course\">CFP Board capstone guidance</a></p>"},{"id":"cfp-class-7-8","title":"Course 7 · Class 8 · Draft estate and succession actions","html":"<h3>Course 7 · Class 8 · Draft estate and succession actions</h3><p><a href=\"#cfp-class-7-7\">Previous class</a> · <a href=\"#capstone\">Course syllabus</a> · <a href=\"#cfp-class-7-9\">Next class</a></p><h4>Two-hour class</h4><ol><li>10 minutes · Recall what you learned in the previous class or identify what you already know.</li><li>35 minutes · Learn the concepts using the linked topic lessons. Answer each knowledge check before revealing the answer.</li><li>25 minutes · Work through the linked topic questions. Write down the rule, inputs and interpretation.</li><li>10 minutes · Break.</li><li>30 minutes · Complete the class assignment. Explain what changes if an assumption is wrong.</li><li>10 minutes · Explain your conclusion aloud, log anything you missed and mark the class complete.</li></ol><h4>Teaching and worked practice</h4><ul><li><a href=\"#topic-54\">Open Topic 54</a></li><li><a href=\"#topic-56\">Open Topic 56</a></li><li><a href=\"#topic-58\">Open Topic 58</a></li></ul><h4>Class assignment</h4><p>Trace beneficiaries, available cash and which decisions go to counsel.</p><p><a href=\"#capstone\">Open the Rivera capstone and rubric</a> · <a href=\"#workbook\">Open the advisor worksheets</a></p><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.cfp.net/certification-process/education-requirement/certification-coursework-requirement/the-capstone-course\">CFP Board capstone guidance</a></p>"},{"id":"cfp-class-7-9","title":"Course 7 · Class 9 · Integrate, implement and monitor","html":"<h3>Course 7 · Class 9 · Integrate, implement and monitor</h3><p><a href=\"#cfp-class-7-8\">Previous class</a> · <a href=\"#capstone\">Course syllabus</a> · <a href=\"#cfp-class-7-10\">Next class</a></p><h4>Two-hour class</h4><ol><li>10 minutes · Recall what you learned in the previous class or identify what you already know.</li><li>35 minutes · Learn the concepts using the lesson below and the linked topic lessons. Answer each knowledge check before revealing the answer.</li><li>25 minutes · Work through the example below. Write down the rule, inputs and interpretation.</li><li>10 minutes · Break.</li><li>30 minutes · Complete the class assignment. Explain what changes if an assumption is wrong.</li><li>10 minutes · Explain your conclusion aloud, log anything you missed and mark the class complete.</li></ol><h4>Integrate the plan and present the recommendation</h4><p>Use a case file, calculation workbook and client meeting script. Start with a written scope and verified facts. Rank goals, compare a baseline with alternatives, and explain the impact across insurance, taxes, investments, retirement and estate planning. Show assumptions next to results. Finish each action with the responsible person, due date and the trigger for review.</p><h4>Worked example</h4><p>A family has $1,500 of monthly surplus, high-interest card debt, a reserve gap and an upcoming tuition bill. Compare a $1,000 debt and $500 reserve split against a reserve-first plan. Show how both choices affect liquidity and interest. Address risks you can mitigate without immediate spending, such as confirming beneficiary forms and employer benefits. Estimate later cash available for tuition and retirement after the card is paid. Present the preferred path and one downside in plain language.</p><h4>Practice variation</h4><p>Prepare a one-page plan using the capstone facts. Include two alternatives, a calculation with assumptions, a 90-day action list and a monitoring trigger. How do you know the plan is ready to present?</p><details><summary>Check your work</summary><p>Check that every dollar is allocated once, each number can be traced to a fact or assumption, risks and conflicts are disclosed, and each recommendation has an owner and date. A client should be able to explain the trade-off back to you.</p></details><h4>Related topic lessons</h4><ul><li><a href=\"#topic-6\">Open Topic 6</a></li><li><a href=\"#topic-7\">Open Topic 7</a></li><li><a href=\"#topic-69\">Open Topic 69</a></li></ul><h4>Class assignment</h4><p>Create the 90-day plan with owners, deadlines, metrics and review triggers.</p><p><a href=\"#capstone\">Open the Rivera capstone and rubric</a> · <a href=\"#workbook\">Open the advisor worksheets</a></p><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.cfp.net/certification-process/education-requirement/certification-coursework-requirement/the-capstone-course\">CFP Board capstone guidance</a></p>"},{"id":"cfp-class-7-10","title":"Course 7 · Class 10 · Present and defend the plan","html":"<h3>Course 7 · Class 10 · Present and defend the plan</h3><p><a href=\"#cfp-class-7-9\">Previous class</a> · <a href=\"#capstone\">Course syllabus</a></p><h4>Two-hour class</h4><ol><li>10 minutes · Recall what you learned in the previous class or identify what you already know.</li><li>35 minutes · Learn the concepts using the linked topic lessons. Answer each knowledge check before revealing the answer.</li><li>25 minutes · Work through the linked topic questions. Write down the rule, inputs and interpretation.</li><li>10 minutes · Break.</li><li>30 minutes · Complete the class assignment. Explain what changes if an assumption is wrong.</li><li>10 minutes · Explain your conclusion aloud, log anything you missed and mark the class complete.</li></ol><h4>Teaching and worked practice</h4><ul><li><a href=\"#topic-7\">Open Topic 7</a></li><li><a href=\"#topic-67\">Open Topic 67</a></li><li><a href=\"#topic-69\">Open Topic 69</a></li></ul><h4>Class assignment</h4><p>Deliver a five-minute client presentation, ask for teach-back and score the work with the capstone rubric.</p><p><a href=\"#capstone\">Open the Rivera capstone and rubric</a> · <a href=\"#workbook\">Open the advisor worksheets</a></p><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.cfp.net/certification-process/education-requirement/certification-coursework-requirement/the-capstone-course\">CFP Board capstone guidance</a></p>"}]'::jsonb;
  previous jsonb;
  updated jsonb;
BEGIN
  SELECT lessons INTO STRICT previous FROM public.tac_academy_courses WHERE slug='financial-planning-cfp-prep' FOR UPDATE;
  IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM jsonb_object_keys(syllabus) AS series(id)
    WHERE (SELECT count(*) FROM jsonb_array_elements(previous) AS l WHERE l->>'id'=series.id) <> 1)
    OR (SELECT count(*) FROM jsonb_array_elements(previous) AS l WHERE l->>'id' ~ '^topic-[0-9]+$') <> 70
    OR NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM jsonb_array_elements(previous) AS l WHERE l->>'id'='workbook')
  THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'CFP course targets do not match';
  END IF;

  SELECT jsonb_agg(entry ORDER BY seq, position) INTO updated
  FROM (
    SELECT n AS seq, 0 AS position, 
      CASE WHEN syllabus ? (l->>'id') AND strpos(l->>'html', syllabus->>(l->>'id'))=0 THEN
        jsonb_set(l, '{html}', to_jsonb(
          left(l->>'html', strpos(l->>'html','</h3>')+4)
          || (syllabus->>(l->>'id'))
          || substr(l->>'html', strpos(l->>'html','</h3>')+5)
        ))
      ELSE l END AS entry
      FROM jsonb_array_elements(previous) WITH ORDINALITY AS old(l,n) WHERE l->>'id' NOT LIKE 'cfp-class-%'
    UNION ALL
    SELECT course.n, slot, class
      FROM jsonb_array_elements(previous) WITH ORDINALITY AS course(l,n)
      JOIN jsonb_array_elements(classes) WITH ORDINALITY AS lesson(class,slot)
      ON course.l->>'id'=CASE WHEN split_part(class->>'id','-',3)='7' THEN 'capstone' ELSE 'course-'||split_part(class->>'id','-',3) END
  ) AS ordered;
  IF jsonb_array_length(updated) <> (SELECT count(*) FROM jsonb_array_elements(previous) AS l WHERE l->>'id' NOT LIKE 'cfp-class-%') + 70
    THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'CFP class count mismatch';
  END IF;
  UPDATE public.tac_academy_courses SET lessons=updated WHERE slug='financial-planning-cfp-prep';
END;
$$;
COMMIT;
